       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Common adult oral regimens are:\n- **Standard analgesic or anti-inflammatory:** 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, up to 3,200 mg/day.\n- **Total of 1,600 mg/day:** 400 mg four times daily.\n\nBecause this is a prescribing decision, I'd like a licensed prescriber on the medicine service to confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once a prescriber gives me the corrected order, for example 800 mg by mouth three times daily or 400 mg four times daily, I can enter it right away."
